<title>UK: Four companies share BSkyB box order.</title>
<headline>Four companies share BSkyB box order.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>British Sky Broadcasting Plc said on Wednesday it had divided its order for a total of one million digital television set-top boxes between four companies.</p>
<p>The four are Amstrad, Pace Micro Technology Plc, Matsushita and Grundig/Hyundai.</p>
<p>BSkyB plans to launch 200-channel digital satellite TV services into the UK in spring 1998. New interactive services such as home shopping are expected to become available shortly afterwards.</p>
<p>BSkyB, BT, Matushita and Midland Bank have joined forces to create a new company to deliver interactive services to UK viewers. They plan to subsidise the boxes down to a retail price of about 200 pounds.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
